  "foot": "⚙️ CPRP · CNC Machining & Quality — B1+ · self-marking 📐",
  "story": [
    "Théo is a <span class=\"hl\">machining apprentice</span>. This week, he <span class=\"hl\">sets up</span> a new <span class=\"hl\">CNC lathe</span> to produce a series of steel shafts. First, the <span class=\"hl\">blank</span> is clamped in the <span class=\"hl\">chuck</span>. A carbide <span class=\"hl\">cutting tool</span> removes the metal, and the diameter <span class=\"hl\">is turned</span> to size. During the operation, the <span class=\"hl\">coolant</span> cools the tool and the <span class=\"hl\">chips</span> fall into the tray. Every movement <span class=\"hl\">is controlled</span> by the CNC program.",
    "First, the operator loads the blank and starts the cycle. <span class=\"hl\">As soon as</span> the <span class=\"hl\">spindle</span> reaches full speed, the tool moves in and the first cut begins. <span class=\"hl\">Subsequently</span>, the machine turns the second diameter and drills the center hole. When the program is finished, the part is unloaded; <span class=\"hl\">therefore</span> the next blank can be machined. If a dimension is out of <span class=\"hl\">tolerance</span>, the part is sent to <span class=\"hl\">scrap</span>.",
    "Safety comes first. Théo <span class=\"hl\">must</span> stop the spindle before he opens the guard, and operators <span class=\"hl\">mustn't</span> remove a safety cover. After machining, each shaft <span class=\"hl\">is deburred</span> and measured with a <span class=\"hl\">caliper</span> and a <span class=\"hl\">micrometer</span>. If the operator presses the <span class=\"hl\">emergency stop</span>, the machine <span class=\"hl\">will stop</span> immediately. Since Monday, Théo has inspected every part, and the batch has passed quality control without a single reject. ⚙️"
  ],
